{"causes": ["The marriage of his father, Rostislav Mikhailovich, to Anna of Hungary provided the familial and political basis for his claim to Hungarian ducal territories.", "The ongoing internal conflicts within the Árpád dynasty, particularly between King Béla IV and his son Stephen V, created opportunities and challenges for regional rulers like Béla of Macsó.", "The strategic importance of the southern Hungarian marches as a buffer against external threats and a source of resources necessitated strong ducal leadership."], "effects": ["Béla's death at the Battle of Hód-tó contributed to the destabilization of the southern Hungarian marches, leading to increased magnate power.", "The fragmentation of the Duchy of Macsó and Bosnia after his death weakened Hungarian control over the Balkans for decades.", "His legacy highlights the precarious nature of royal authority in frontier regions during periods of internal dynastic strife in medieval Hungary."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "rostislav-mikhailovich", "sourceName": "Rostislav Mikhailovich", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "bla-of-macs", "targetName": "Béla of Macsó", "context": "Béla of Macsó inherited the Duchy of Macsó and Bosnia from his father, Rostislav Mikhailovich, who established a strong dynastic presence in the region."}, {"sourceSlug": "bla-of-macs", "sourceName": "Béla of Macsó", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "battle-of-hod-to", "targetName": "Battle of Hód-tó", "context": "Béla of Macsó died on November 1, 1272, fighting alongside King Stephen V against rebellious nobles at the Battle of Hód-tó."}, {"sourceSlug": "bla-of-macs", "sourceName": "Béla of Macsó", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "kingdom-of-hungary", "targetName": "Kingdom of Hungary", "context": "Béla of Macsó governed the southern provinces of Macsó and Bosnia as a duke within the Kingdom of Hungary from 1262 to 1272."}, {"sourceSlug": "stephen-v-of-hungary", "sourceName": "Stephen V of Hungary", "verb": "COLLABO